{"key":"AppGalleryWindow","text":"## AppGalleryWindow\n\nThe **App Gallery** is the built-in app launcher and dock-pinning interface.\nIt is always pinned as the leftmost icon in the dock and cannot be removed.\n\n---\n\n@layout\nTitle Bar | 0.50, 0.04 | The App Gallery is the built-in app launcher. It is always pinned as the leftmost dock icon and cannot be removed.\nApp Grid | 0.50, 0.55 | Scrollable grid of all available apps. Single-click to open (or restore) an app. Click-and-hold then drag to the dock bar to pin it, or drag to the desktop to create a shortcut. Icons load asynchronously from GitHub.\n\n---\n\n### Opening Apps\n\n- **Single click** an app tile to open it (or restore its window if already open)\n\n---\n\n### Pinning to the Dock\n\n1. **Click-and-hold** an app tile until the drag starts\n2. A ghost icon with a **+ Pin to Dock** label follows the cursor\n3. Drag to the **dock bar** at the bottom of the screen\n4. An animated spacer shows where the icon will land\n5. Release to pin the app permanently\n\n---\n\n### Adding a Desktop Shortcut\n\n1. **Click-and-hold** an app tile\n2. Drag to the **desktop background** area (not the dock)\n3. The ghost label changes to **+ Add to Desktop**\n4. Release to create a shortcut icon on the desktop\n\n---\n\n### Icon Loading\n\nApp icons are loaded asynchronously from GitHub.  A placeholder is shown\nuntil the real icon downloads. Icons are cached for the session.\n\n---","screenshot":""}